			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Rebuild compiled output after RouteManifest regeneration\n\nRegenerate RouteManifest timestamp and rebuild all Target/ artifacts (JS bundles and source maps). This pass also removes a stale deprecation warning from the `MountainGRPCClientService` JSDoc in `Client.ts`, reflecting the conclusion of the gRPC service layer transition.\n\nMountain method count remains at 142.",
			"SHA": "59e5300940bc2ca4c8b2c2a397c1b925f95d511a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T18:19:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1191,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Project SCM command arguments to JSON-safe shape\n\n`SanitizeResourceState` was stripping `arguments` from SCM command objects entirely, under the assumption that the workbench resolves arguments by command id at execution time. However, `git.openChange` and `git.openFile` handlers in vscode.git read `args[0].resourceUri` to determine which file to diff — without the projected resource handle, clicking a file in the SCM list silently opened the wrong file or nothing at all.\n\nReplace the blanket `arguments` strip with a `ProjectArg` function that shallow-copies each argument and preserves only the safe primitive fields the diff handler actually consults: `resourceUri`, URI POJO fields (`scheme`, `authority`, `path`, `query`, `fragment`), `fsPath`, `external`, and scalar metadata (`type`, `originalUri`, `renameUri`, `contextValue`, `id`). vscode.git's Repository back-reference (the cycle root) is naturally excluded since it is an object with none of these scalar keys.\n\nSCM resource commands now correctly navigate to the intended file across all git integration features.",
			"SHA": "ab7a526b8fda6b5d38ce12d3ab078f12c732d768"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T17:58:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1191,
				37
			],
			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Rebuild compiled output after RouteManifest regeneration\n\nRegenerate RouteManifest timestamp and rebuild all Target/ artifacts (JS bundles and source maps) following handler code changes. Mountain method count remains at 142 — no new RPC methods were added in this pass.\n\nThe rebuild ensures the bootstrap, service, handler, and gRPC bundles in Target/ are consistent with the regenerated RouteManifest.",
			"SHA": "8b2417341ef3d747def570378863a1f942d6322a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T17:58:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1191,
				83
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Build full TextDocument shim for all notification handlers\n\nNotification paths `$acceptVisibleEditorsChanged`, `$acceptVisibleRangesChanged`, `$acceptTextEditorOptionsChanged`, `$acceptTextEditorDiffInformation`, and `$acceptTextEditorViewColumn` previously emitted bare `{uri, fileName}` document stubs. Built-in extensions (vscode.git diff decorations, vscode.merge-conflict) iterate the resulting editors and call `.getText()`, `.lineAt()`, `.positionAt()` inside their `applyDecorations` callbacks — the bare stub produced `TypeError: r.getText is not a function`.\n\nAdd `BuildTextDocumentShim` in `Notification/Handler.ts` that returns a full `TextDocument`-shaped object backed by `DocumentContentCache`. Prefers the live entry from `__textDocuments` (the full-fidelity doc kept in sync by `$acceptModelChanged`) and falls back to a content-cache-backed shim implementing `getText`, `lineAt`, `positionAt`, `offsetAt`, `getWordRangeAtPosition`, and `validateRange`. Replace every inline `{document: {uri, fileName}}` stub in the notification dispatch with a `BuildTextDocumentShim` call.\n\nAlso fix `showTextDocument` in `Window/Namespace.ts` to always resolve the URI to a string before sending over IPC — passing the raw document object strips prototype methods (including `toString()`), and the workbench renders the editor tab as `[object Object]`. Add a cascade covering string, vscode.Uri, TextDocument shim, and POJO URI shapes.\n\nFix SCM group update routing in `Scm/Namespace.ts` by including `scmHandle` and `groupHandle` in the `update_scm_group` Mountain request. Without these, multi-repo workspaces sharing `scmId=\"git\"` had updates routed against the wrong provider — Mountain logged `scm_handle=None` and Sky's `ResolveScmShim` fell back to non-unique scmId lookup, silently dropping updates.\n\nRename telemetry config fields in `PostHog/Configuration.ts`: `OTLPEndpoint` → `Pipe`, `OTLPEnabled` → `Emit` for clearer naming.\n\nRegenerate RouteManifest adding two new Mountain RPC methods (`git.openChange`, `git.openFile`), bringing the method count from 140 to 142.",
			"SHA": "1a408045f3e3915b132e6b2d8fd85f68a868ad8d"
		},
